## ADGM Court Procedure Rules 2016 — Rule 24 (summary judgment)
##
## Source: ADGM Court Procedure Rules 2016, Rule 24 (Summary Judgment).
## The court may give summary judgment against a party (claimant or
## defendant) on the whole of a claim, or on a particular issue, if it
## considers that:
##
##   (a) that party has *no realistic prospect of succeeding* on the
##       claim or issue (or, for a defendant, of successfully defending
##       it); AND
##   (b) there is *no other compelling reason* why the case or issue
##       should be disposed of at trial.
##
## Both limbs must be satisfied — the test is conjunctive. The "no
## realistic prospect" limb is read against the *Easyair* gloss
## (ICI Chemicals Industries v Tesco Plc): the prospect must be more
## than fanciful but the court must avoid conducting a mini-trial.
##
## Used by ADGM CFI for early disposal across the contract-dispute
## docket. Reciprocal in shape to DIFC RDC Rule 24 (which uses the
## identical English-CPR-derived test).
##
## Applies in:
##   ADGM contract disputes; default-judgment contests; jurisdictional
##   summary applications.

```catala
declaration structure SummaryJudgmentApplication:
  data no_realistic_prospect content boolean
  data no_compelling_reason content boolean

declaration structure SummaryJudgmentDisposition:
  data both_limbs_made_out content boolean
  data summary_judgment_granted content boolean

declaration scope SummaryJudgmentTest:
  input application content SummaryJudgmentApplication
  output disposition content SummaryJudgmentDisposition

scope SummaryJudgmentTest:
  definition disposition equals
    let both equals
      application.no_realistic_prospect
      and application.no_compelling_reason
    in
    SummaryJudgmentDisposition {
      -- both_limbs_made_out: both
      -- summary_judgment_granted: both
    }
```

## Tests — both limbs convolved.

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestSummaryJudgmentBothLimbs:
  composite scope SummaryJudgmentTest
  output disposition content SummaryJudgmentDisposition

scope TestSummaryJudgmentBothLimbs:
  definition disposition equals composite.disposition
  definition composite.application equals
    SummaryJudgmentApplication {
      -- no_realistic_prospect: true
      -- no_compelling_reason: true
    }
  assertion disposition.summary_judgment_granted = true

#[test] declaration scope TestSummaryJudgmentRefusedOnCompellingReason:
  composite scope SummaryJudgmentTest
  output disposition content SummaryJudgmentDisposition

scope TestSummaryJudgmentRefusedOnCompellingReason:
  definition disposition equals composite.disposition
  ## Even where the prospect limb is made out, a compelling reason for
  ## trial (e.g. credibility issues that need cross-examination) is
  ## sufficient to refuse summary judgment.
  definition composite.application equals
    SummaryJudgmentApplication {
      -- no_realistic_prospect: true
      -- no_compelling_reason: false
    }
  assertion disposition.summary_judgment_granted = false
```
